WEBVTT

00:00:17.620 --> 00:00:23.670
Are you Ledell Nikolavitch, one of the world's top 5 snipers?

00:00:23.670 --> 00:00:25.080
Top 5?

00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:30.670
I don't know about the other four, but I'm myself and that's enough.

00:00:30.670 --> 00:00:32.050
I see.

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:34.430
Your confidence is first rate too, I see.

00:00:36.590 --> 00:00:41.180
Take a look - there's a target about 600 meters from here.

00:00:42.430 --> 00:00:46.940
Put a bullet into the forehead of the fore target.

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:50.320
The target behind it is your client.

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:54.150
You mustn't hurt him no matter what.

00:00:55.910 --> 00:01:00.660
I don't like being tested, hit up one of the other four.

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:07.170
We need to maintain our secrecy, you see.

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:09.790
By the way,

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:14.050
two other people have already failed this audition before me.

00:01:14.050 --> 00:01:14.840
What?

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:18.850
Don't make us dig another hole around here.

00:01:34.990 --> 00:01:36.490
Shot 5 is successful.

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:39.740
Shot 6 is successful.

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:42.240
Shot 7 is successful.

00:01:44.290 --> 00:01:45.250
Shot 8 is successful.

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:49.330
Shot 9 is successful.

00:01:53.590 --> 00:01:54.510
What's wrong?

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:57.090
Give that to me.

00:01:57.090 --> 00:01:58.930
How did he do?

00:01:58.930 --> 00:02:00.090
Respond!

00:02:01.050 --> 00:02:06.850
I'm risking my life sniping, I saw a fly in my scope.

00:02:15.110 --> 00:02:17.280
Very well, you're hired.

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:21.910
Ted Conan. We want you to eliminate him.

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:44.260
I held my breath and kept waiting while my heart was scratched away

00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:55.610
A minute, a second never felt so long

00:02:56.110 --> 00:03:07.370
I look up at the sky and ask the wind, "Can I fly now?"

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:13.670
The weak person I was is no more

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:19.260
I decided to just believe

00:03:20.590 --> 00:03:26.390
With the dreams I once had in my hand now

00:03:26.390 --> 00:03:30.230
I go towards you

00:03:32.150 --> 00:03:37.940
Carrying those emotions I felt when I broke

00:03:37.940 --> 00:03:42.070
I go towards you

00:03:42.070 --> 00:03:46.120
Blown by the wind

00:03:46.870 --> 00:03:51.580
Oh blown

00:03:54.250 --> 00:03:58.340
The Superstar's Joint Appearance

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:59.050
To bite the hand that feeds you is an appropriate term.

00:04:00.170 --> 00:04:02.800
I have no relatives.

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:06.050
So I thought of him as my son.

00:04:06.050 --> 00:04:08.810
I taught him all there is to know about the business,

00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:11.890
and he's now the vice president of my company.

00:04:11.890 --> 00:04:13.850
And yet, he...

00:04:13.850 --> 00:04:16.150
I have no interest in my client's circumstances.

00:04:17.150 --> 00:04:19.070
Please get to the point.

00:04:19.070 --> 00:04:21.440
Sorry.

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:24.410
This is what happens when you get old.

00:04:25.950 --> 00:04:29.870
Bob hired a certain man to get rid of me.

00:04:29.870 --> 00:04:31.910
This is Bob.

00:04:35.330 --> 00:04:36.830
Allow me to introduce:

00:04:36.830 --> 00:04:43.800
the man who planned and created this work, vice president of Conan Associates, Bob Stigner.

00:04:47.640 --> 00:04:49.390
Thank you, everyone.

00:04:49.390 --> 00:04:50.430
Thank you, really.

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:56.520
But I cannot accept this alone.

00:04:56.520 --> 00:05:00.440
The glory from this success is all because of a certain person,

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:07.450
the man who raised the American show business, and my beloved teacher, president Ted Conan.

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:12.450
I wouldn't be where I am today without his teachings.

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:15.460
Kill Bob.

00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:20.800
But I wouldn't ask you just to kill him, I wouldn't bother hiring you for that.

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:24.470
That's not enough for me.

00:05:24.470 --> 00:05:29.010
So there's one major condition you must consider.

00:05:29.010 --> 00:05:33.850
I want you to kill Bob just before I am shot.

00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:38.480
He'll die at the time when I was supposed to die.

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:43.820
The assassin he hired is one of the finest snipers in the world.

00:05:43.820 --> 00:05:49.950
But this is to my advantage, it shows what he plans to do.

00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:57.870
In one week I will fly to Chicago for the All-American Producers Summit.

00:05:57.870 --> 00:06:04.920
I imagine he will aim for the moment when I depart from my plane at O'Hare.

00:06:04.920 --> 00:06:06.340
How do you know?

00:06:06.340 --> 00:06:10.510
His goal is to replace me.

00:06:10.930 --> 00:06:14.180
If he eliminates me just before the summit,

00:06:14.180 --> 00:06:19.060
he'll be able to attend it as the representative of Conan Associates.

00:06:19.060 --> 00:06:23.020
He's trying to create that established fact.

00:06:23.020 --> 00:06:25.280
Who is the sniper he hired?

00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:27.530
Ledell Nikolavitch,

00:06:28.150 --> 00:06:33.700
the favored winner of the Olympic medal for small bore rifles.

00:06:33.700 --> 00:06:41.790
But he needed money and started taking underworld jobs, and vanished from the public eye.

00:06:44.210 --> 00:06:50.590
He uses a modified Mauser rifle.

00:06:50.590 --> 00:06:58.810
To minimize the recoil he uses an electronic primer with a lock time of zero.

00:06:58.810 --> 00:07:04.650
He's set the trigger to be as sensitive as physically possible.

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:10.610
It's said that he's an especially good sniper in the kneeling position.

00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:12.660
I'm sorry.

00:07:12.660 --> 00:07:15.080
I forget who I'm talking to.

00:07:15.080 --> 00:07:17.200
I'd like you to contact me with this in the future.

00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:19.330
The reward is 3 million dollars.

00:07:19.330 --> 00:07:21.420
Will you take it?

00:07:22.250 --> 00:07:23.330
I shall.

00:07:25.380 --> 00:07:28.340
Thank you, Mr. Tougou.

00:07:38.930 --> 00:07:40.060
It's Stigner.

00:07:40.690 --> 00:07:41.640
Alright.

00:07:41.640 --> 00:07:42.850
Put him through.

00:07:44.730 --> 00:07:46.820
It's halftime.

00:07:46.820 --> 00:07:48.570
I'll call you later.

00:08:02.830 --> 00:08:05.130
That was Elanor Lane, right?

00:08:05.130 --> 00:08:07.960
Is it okay to touch your own product?

00:08:07.960 --> 00:08:09.090
Thanks.

00:08:10.300 --> 00:08:12.510
We're not planning on keeping her.

00:08:12.510 --> 00:08:17.680
Of course, the president always tells me not to touch the merchandise.

00:08:22.810 --> 00:08:23.480
Well?

00:08:23.480 --> 00:08:26.480
You're sure about the skills of the man you hired, right?

00:08:26.480 --> 00:08:28.400
His skills are the best.

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:29.900
He's a bit stubborn, though.

00:08:29.900 --> 00:08:32.900
Kill him when the job's done.

00:08:32.900 --> 00:08:35.700
I'm not sure which of us is the mafia.

00:08:38.700 --> 00:08:40.870
100 Top men from around the world?

00:08:40.870 --> 00:08:42.960
King of Broadway.

00:08:44.500 --> 00:08:49.170
Funny since they're going to be putting out a memorial on him next month.

00:08:50.710 --> 00:08:51.630
Bob?

00:08:52.260 --> 00:08:54.180
We're done talking about work.

00:08:54.840 --> 00:08:55.840
Leave.

00:09:00.260 --> 00:09:03.140
Did I say something wrong?

00:09:03.140 --> 00:09:05.020
I'm just a kid.

00:09:05.020 --> 00:09:06.100
Don't worry about it.

00:09:06.100 --> 00:09:07.610
Very well.

00:09:34.470 --> 00:09:35.930
Now look at the camera.

00:09:35.930 --> 00:09:37.470
Yeah.

00:09:37.470 --> 00:09:40.350
Nobody wants to see a pose like that.

00:09:40.850 --> 00:09:43.430
You need to hide her sexiness and hint at it!

00:09:43.430 --> 00:09:45.350
It's almost as if he thinks he's the president.

00:09:45.350 --> 00:09:47.350
It's almost time for a changing of the guard, huh?

00:09:47.350 --> 00:09:48.440
Next.

00:09:48.440 --> 00:09:50.440
Elena, take your jeans off.

00:09:55.400 --> 00:09:56.860
Assholes...

00:09:56.860 --> 00:09:59.660
If I had the cash...

00:09:59.660 --> 00:10:04.750
If I had the cash I could make a hit or two.

00:10:06.370 --> 00:10:11.210
So you thought if you had the cash, people would come see your play?

00:10:15.590 --> 00:10:17.050
Who the hell are you?

00:10:17.630 --> 00:10:23.100
You don't notice your inexperience and just blame it on the money... You'll be third-rate forever.

00:10:23.100 --> 00:10:24.600
What?

00:10:26.850 --> 00:10:32.690
Write in the number you need and then make a hit show.

00:10:34.820 --> 00:10:35.990
What's wrong?

00:10:35.990 --> 00:10:38.570
Won't you be able to succeed as long as you have the money?

00:10:42.870 --> 00:10:44.790
Yeah, I'll make the money.

00:10:44.790 --> 00:10:46.580
I'll make as much as you want!

00:10:46.580 --> 00:10:52.130
Then pay me back in six months,
with interest, for as much as you wrote.

00:10:52.130 --> 00:10:54.000
If you can't...

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:55.880
If I can't...

00:10:55.880 --> 00:10:58.880
You'll work for me to pay off your debt.

00:10:59.880 --> 00:11:02.550
And Bob failed.

00:11:03.390 --> 00:11:06.390
But I knew it.

00:11:06.810 --> 00:11:11.020
He was useless the way he was, but he had potential.

00:11:11.020 --> 00:11:12.980
If I trained him.

00:11:13.860 --> 00:11:15.770
And I was right.

00:11:18.490 --> 00:11:19.700
It's been a while.

00:11:19.700 --> 00:11:21.110
Thought you were dead.

00:11:21.110 --> 00:11:24.120
If I was dead it'd get an article in the paper.

00:11:29.160 --> 00:11:30.460
Never seen him before.

00:11:30.460 --> 00:11:32.120
He was here yesterday, too.

00:11:37.380 --> 00:11:39.670
Can I sit next to you?

00:11:39.670 --> 00:11:43.760
This ain't a spot for tourists.

00:11:43.760 --> 00:11:45.550
You Asian?

00:11:45.550 --> 00:11:46.970
I'm from Poland.

00:11:46.970 --> 00:11:48.720
Name's Nikolavitch.

00:11:52.520 --> 00:11:54.560
You're not very friendly.

00:11:57.320 --> 00:11:58.690
One more.

00:12:01.200 --> 00:12:05.320
I was in the army once; it was a terrible place.

00:12:05.320 --> 00:12:09.200
It was the shots from your own side, not the enemy, that you had to worry about.

00:12:09.200 --> 00:12:14.710
I was the one who shot, not who got shot at.

00:12:15.580 --> 00:12:17.170
You talk too much.

00:12:25.840 --> 00:12:29.100
A man who never shakes with his dominant hand.

00:12:30.600 --> 00:12:33.730
An Asian who never smiles.

00:12:33.730 --> 00:12:35.100
It can't be...

00:12:35.690 --> 00:12:37.110
He can't be...

00:12:56.750 --> 00:12:59.420
Sniping isn't my specialty, but...

00:13:01.880 --> 00:13:04.970
The guy from the Olympic preliminaries, right?

00:13:04.970 --> 00:13:07.850
The image is pretty bad, is it an 8mm?

00:13:09.560 --> 00:13:12.350
This is military sniper training, huh?

00:13:12.350 --> 00:13:16.730
Oh, this is footage from the Foreign Minister Grahm assassination, isn't it?

00:13:16.730 --> 00:13:18.360
He was involved in that?

00:13:20.360 --> 00:13:21.570
From there.

00:13:22.360 --> 00:13:23.940
Slow it down.

00:13:31.950 --> 00:13:39.960
He lowers the sight from above in a relaxed position and fires after slowly rotating his right elbow, huh?

00:13:39.960 --> 00:13:45.880
It's very slight, but he lowers his sight after rotating his right elbow.

00:13:46.550 --> 00:13:51.720
I can see him rotating his elbow, but the gun isn't moving!

00:13:51.720 --> 00:13:57.690
In terms of angle, it would be 6 thousandths of an inch, in other words, less than a third of a degree.

00:14:08.200 --> 00:14:09.070
Here.

00:14:13.160 --> 00:14:16.870
You can see such slight movements?

00:14:16.870 --> 00:14:22.420
I want you to analyze this angle, and with an accuracy of 1/60th.

00:14:23.210 --> 00:14:24.460
Impossible...

00:14:24.460 --> 00:14:26.010
Even if he did it,

00:14:26.010 --> 00:14:31.930
a third of a degree translates to a 58 centimeter difference in end points at 100 meters away!

00:14:32.430 --> 00:14:38.940
What I'm after is the angle needed to generate a 53 centimeter difference at a 590 meter distance.

00:14:41.360 --> 00:14:42.940
50,000 dollars.

00:14:42.940 --> 00:14:45.650
Okay, I'll do my best.

00:14:52.950 --> 00:14:54.450
I refuse.

00:14:57.200 --> 00:14:59.420
There's no need to take him out.

00:14:59.420 --> 00:15:02.500
Golgo can't aim at Bob at that airport.

00:15:03.960 --> 00:15:05.460
Do what you want.

00:15:12.220 --> 00:15:13.470
Thank you.

00:15:13.470 --> 00:15:15.260
Excuse me.

00:15:15.260 --> 00:15:16.680
She's a good girl.

00:15:16.680 --> 00:15:18.230
Shall I send a scout over?

00:15:18.230 --> 00:15:20.560
You never change.

00:15:21.310 --> 00:15:23.230
No, nothing.

00:15:25.150 --> 00:15:27.780
You mean the actress.

00:15:28.320 --> 00:15:35.830
I get a lot of stress in this job and wanted somebody to listen to my complaints, but the police

00:15:35.830 --> 00:15:40.710
It's been a long time... since we've eaten together.

00:15:41.830 --> 00:15:43.250
That's true.

00:15:44.670 --> 00:15:47.460
We'll be in Chicago the day after tomorrow.

00:15:47.460 --> 00:15:49.590
How are your preparations proceeding?

00:15:49.590 --> 00:15:51.260
There are no problems.

00:15:51.680 --> 00:15:52.630
I see.

00:15:52.630 --> 00:15:54.470
That's good.

00:15:56.220 --> 00:15:58.470
It was a huge success.

00:15:58.470 --> 00:16:00.600
Thanks. It was all because of you guys.

00:16:00.600 --> 00:16:01.770
President!

00:16:02.390 --> 00:16:05.310
Why are you smiling?

00:16:05.310 --> 00:16:09.030
I can't do much more right now,
but this is a token of my appreciation.

00:16:12.530 --> 00:16:13.990
What a nice necktie.

00:16:13.990 --> 00:16:15.120
Thank you.

00:16:15.120 --> 00:16:17.280
I look forward to working with you.

00:16:18.160 --> 00:16:20.290
Do you remember this?

00:16:21.790 --> 00:16:24.500
How about a refill?

00:16:24.500 --> 00:16:26.130
No, we're fine.

00:16:26.130 --> 00:16:27.630
Excuse me.

00:16:28.170 --> 00:16:29.510
What is that?

00:16:29.510 --> 00:16:31.590
No, never mind.

00:17:05.080 --> 00:17:06.170
Is it done?

00:17:06.630 --> 00:17:08.420
Yeah, somehow.

00:17:08.420 --> 00:17:10.170
First, look at this.

00:17:22.020 --> 00:17:23.680
You're mine this time.

00:17:23.680 --> 00:17:24.480
We'll see.

00:17:24.980 --> 00:17:25.810
Take that!

00:17:25.810 --> 00:17:27.810
Here, here!

00:17:27.810 --> 00:17:28.360
Hey!

00:17:28.360 --> 00:17:28.980
There!

00:17:28.980 --> 00:17:29.570
What are you doing-

00:17:29.570 --> 00:17:30.150
Ah, dammit!

00:17:30.150 --> 00:17:31.940
Hey, what are you doing?

00:17:31.940 --> 00:17:33.110
You're doing it wrong!

00:17:33.110 --> 00:17:33.860
Okay, let's go!

00:17:33.860 --> 00:17:34.990
All right, one more time!

00:17:35.780 --> 00:17:36.410
Go!

00:17:36.910 --> 00:17:38.660
Hey, over here!

00:17:38.660 --> 00:17:39.780
It's mine!

00:17:41.330 --> 00:17:42.160
Take that!

00:17:41.660 --> 00:17:43.200
Okay, one more time!

00:17:43.200 --> 00:17:43.620
Alright.

00:17:43.620 --> 00:17:44.160
Yeah.

00:17:44.160 --> 00:17:44.710
Let's go!

00:17:44.710 --> 00:17:45.290
Here.

00:17:47.120 --> 00:17:48.000
Okay, here-

00:17:56.800 --> 00:17:59.090
I want you to check this license plate.

00:17:59.090 --> 00:18:00.800
2447HI.

00:18:00.800 --> 00:18:02.140
There are four victims.

00:18:02.140 --> 00:18:04.770
We've only found the identity of one: Al Trayton, age 44.

00:18:04.770 --> 00:18:06.850
He's a higher up in the Italian mafia.

00:18:06.850 --> 00:18:10.810
We've found another victim in an alley 200 meters away.

00:18:10.810 --> 00:18:12.270
He's been shot through the forehead.

00:18:12.270 --> 00:18:13.360
Roger.

00:18:25.080 --> 00:18:28.710
I'm going to Chicago as planned tomorrow.

00:18:31.040 --> 00:18:33.840
This is my last call to you.

00:18:35.670 --> 00:18:38.680
Yesterday, I had dinner with Bob.

00:18:40.300 --> 00:18:42.260
I'm counting on you.

00:18:42.260 --> 00:18:43.350
Understood.

00:18:46.770 --> 00:18:51.860
This conference is an established place for making an appearance, but...

00:18:53.020 --> 00:18:54.480
President?

00:18:54.480 --> 00:18:55.860
Are you listening?

00:18:56.900 --> 00:18:58.360
Sorry, sorry.

00:18:58.360 --> 00:19:00.610
I was thinking.

00:19:02.620 --> 00:19:05.830
I'm getting old.

00:19:05.830 --> 00:19:10.080
For many years there was nobody in my company to take my place,

00:19:10.080 --> 00:19:14.840
or rather, I've been the president to represent the company.

00:19:14.840 --> 00:19:19.510
But I think it's time for me to leave the stage.

00:19:19.510 --> 00:19:23.850
You're the youngest of the company's four vice-presidents,

00:19:24.430 --> 00:19:29.600
but I think you're the only one who has a chance of making it succeed from here on out.

00:19:32.060 --> 00:19:35.860
Make a plan for the conference today.

00:19:47.990 --> 00:19:50.870
There's no sniper point except this one.

00:19:51.870 --> 00:19:56.380
As long as I'm here, it's impossible for Golgo to take out Bob.

00:20:18.230 --> 00:20:23.860
When he holds his gun, the angle is off 0 degrees and 3 minutes.

00:20:25.910 --> 00:20:30.950
This translates to 2.237 meters above the target.

00:20:31.790 --> 00:20:39.800
The sight lowers at an almost uniform velocity, stopping 1.3 seconds later, and he fires 1.45 seconds later.

00:20:40.960 --> 00:20:48.970
He passes 53 centimeters above the target one 1/100th of a second before frame 26,

00:20:48.970 --> 00:20:52.730
in other words, .99 seconds after he starts.

00:20:57.650 --> 00:21:01.610
This will undoubtedly be the last time you push me.

00:21:01.610 --> 00:21:07.240
The president can't be pushing around someone who's retired.

00:21:07.820 --> 00:21:09.660
That's not true.

00:21:09.660 --> 00:21:14.460
Even if I become the president, I'll stay with you as always.

00:21:24.800 --> 00:21:27.930
What great weather.

00:21:27.930 --> 00:21:33.640
If we went hunting in a good preserve on a day like this, even I could hit something.

00:21:48.990 --> 00:21:50.160
Stinger!

00:21:50.160 --> 00:21:51.120
Vice-president! Vice-president!

00:21:51.120 --> 00:21:52.370
Vice-president! Vice-president!

00:21:58.670 --> 00:22:00.880
Where did he fire from?

00:22:00.880 --> 00:22:02.670
Probably from there...

00:22:07.720 --> 00:22:08.970
Bob...

00:22:08.970 --> 00:22:17.190
There was a time when I really did plan to retire and make you the president.

00:22:42.130 --> 00:22:49.720
Chiisana koto ni zenryoku ni naru kimi no sugata yuuki ni natta hibi

00:22:42.130 --> 00:22:49.720
Those days I saw you giving your all for small things filled me with courage

00:22:49.720 --> 00:22:57.180
Zutto horyuu shippanashi jya ugokenai

00:22:49.720 --> 00:22:57.180
If I keep them suspended then I won't be able to move

00:22:59.190 --> 00:23:06.740
GARASU no HAIWEI ni tatteiru you ni

00:22:59.190 --> 00:23:06.740
It's like I'm standing on a glass highway

00:23:06.740 --> 00:23:13.950
Yume to kiken to senaka awase demo

00:23:06.740 --> 00:23:13.950
Even if I'm standing back to back with dreams and danger

00:23:13.950 --> 00:23:21.080
Kono nagai michi wo sukoshizutsu arukou

00:23:13.950 --> 00:23:21.080
I'll take this long road one step at a time

00:23:21.080 --> 00:23:27.260
Soshite kimi wa ano koro mitai ni

00:23:21.080 --> 00:23:27.260
And I need you to smile

00:23:27.260 --> 00:23:30.260
Waratteite

00:23:27.260 --> 00:23:30.260
Like you did back then

00:23:30.260 --> 00:23:36.890
Shiokaze ni yurete sasayakiatta

00:23:30.260 --> 00:23:36.890
It shook in the sea breeze and whispered

00:23:36.890 --> 00:23:47.480
Kagayaiteita tooi ano hi wa kagerou

00:23:36.890 --> 00:23:47.480
That distant and shining day is a shimmering haze

00:23:45.940 --> 00:23:49.360
The shining days

00:23:50.070 --> 00:23:55.330
Tsumaranai koto ni makeru ni wa hayasugiru

00:23:50.070 --> 00:23:55.330
I can't lose to something so trivial

00:24:01.870 --> 00:24:07.800
Golgo 13 shot a man at the Presidential Nomination Convention.

00:24:07.800 --> 00:24:12.340
The police chase him as a suspect.

00:24:12.340 --> 00:24:13.680
Where did the weapon go?

00:24:13.680 --> 00:24:19.270
And how will Golgo escape?

00:24:19.270 --> 00:24:21.640
Next time on Golgo 13:

00:24:21.140 --> 00:24:27.020
An Offering to God

00:24:21.640 --> 00:24:24.520
An Offering to God.

00:24:24.520 --> 00:24:28.650
Don't stand behind him, if you value your life.
